L248 -- the mass-budget truncation test of the weak-lensing RAR

    loaded 15 RAR bins, g_bar = 1.38e-15 to 3.92e-12 m/s^2
    covariance (15, 15), symmetric to 0.0e+00, diagonal vs quoted errors agree to 0.0%
V1 -- the model-independent version: the slope of the relation at low acceleration
     the square-root branch has log-log slope 1/2; a budget-truncated relation has slope 1 (mass frozen)
    absolute fit of the parameter-free branch: chi2/dof = 13.9 (canonical) / 9.5 (alt) -- NOT a good absolute fit, and it is not claimed to be; everything below is a RELATIVE comparison on identical data
    measured slope over the 8 bins below g_bar = 1e-13 m/s^2: 0.537 +/- 0.026
    distance from the square-root branch (0.5): 1.4 sigma;  from a truncated relation (1.0): 17.6 sigma
  [PASS] V1 [THE RELATION STILL RISES AS A SQUARE ROOT WHERE THE BUDGET SAYS IT MUST HAVE TURNED] the log-log slope of the lensing relation is measured with the full covariance over the bins below 1e-13 m/s^2 and compared with the two predictions: 1/2 for an untruncated square-root branch, 1 for a relation whose enclosed mass has frozen at the galaxies' budget
           (slope = 0.537 +/- 0.026: 17.6 sigma from the truncated value 1, 1.4 sigma from 1/2. The relation has NOT turned over where a bounded mass budget requires it to)

V2 -- the mass budget B = M_dark/M_bar, and the truncation it forces
    log M* = 10.3: abundance-matching M_h = 5.29e+11 M_sun, M_bar = 2.59e+10 -> B = 19.4
    log M* = 10.6: abundance-matching M_h = 1.28e+12 M_sun, M_bar = 5.18e+10 -> B = 23.7
    log M* = 10.8: abundance-matching M_h = 3.41e+12 M_sun, M_bar = 8.20e+10 -> B = 40.6
    log M* = 11.0: abundance-matching M_h = 1.07e+13 M_sun, M_bar = 1.30e+11 -> B = 81.3
    fiducial abundance-matching budget B_AM = 32.1 (median of the four bins)
    cosmic dark-to-baryon ratio B_cosmic = 5.36 (the ratio a fair sample of the universe has)
    [canonical] B_cosmic        B =    5.4: truncation at g_bar = 2.31e-12 m/s^2, 14 of 15 measured bins lie below it
    [canonical] B_AM            B =   32.1: truncation at g_bar = 8.52e-14 m/s^2, 8 of 15 measured bins lie below it
    [canonical] B=100 (stress)  B =  100.0: truncation at g_bar = 9.18e-15 m/s^2, 4 of 15 measured bins lie below it
    [alt] B_cosmic        B =    5.4: truncation at g_bar = 2.78e-12 m/s^2, 14 of 15 measured bins lie below it
    [alt] B_AM            B =   32.1: truncation at g_bar = 1.03e-13 m/s^2, 8 of 15 measured bins lie below it
    [alt] B=100 (stress)  B =  100.0: truncation at g_bar = 1.11e-14 m/s^2, 4 of 15 measured bins lie below it
  [PASS] V2 [THE TRUNCATION FALLS INSIDE THE MEASURED RANGE] the truncation acceleration a_0/(1+B)^2 is computed for the abundance-matching budget and compared with the range the data cover; the test can only bite if bins lie below it
           (B_AM = 32.1 puts the turn at 8.52e-14 m/s^2 with 8 bins below it (canonical); B_cosmic puts it at 2.31e-12 with 14 bins below -- the data reach far enough to see the turn in every budget considered)

V3 -- the truncated model against the data, full covariance
    [canonical] B_cosmic  : chi2 =    1178.2  (untruncated 208.5), Delta chi2 =    +969.7  -> 31.1 sigma against truncation
    [canonical] B_AM      : chi2 =     557.4  (untruncated 208.5), Delta chi2 =    +348.9  -> 18.7 sigma against truncation
    [canonical] B=100     : chi2 =     283.9  (untruncated 208.5), Delta chi2 =     +75.4  -> 8.7 sigma against truncation
    [alt] B_cosmic  : chi2 =    1178.9  (untruncated 143.0), Delta chi2 =   +1035.9  -> 32.2 sigma against truncation
    [alt] B_AM      : chi2 =     528.8  (untruncated 143.0), Delta chi2 =    +385.8  -> 19.6 sigma against truncation
    [alt] B=100     : chi2 =     233.6  (untruncated 143.0), Delta chi2 =     +90.6  -> 9.5 sigma against truncation
  [PASS] V3 [THE TRUNCATED MODEL IS EXCLUDED -- THE PHANTOM IS NOT REAL MASS BOUNDED BY THE HALO BUDGET] the truncated prediction is compared with the untruncated square-root branch on the same data and covariance; a Delta chi-square above 25 (5 sigma) excludes truncation at that budget
           (Delta chi2 = +349 at the abundance-matching budget and +75 even at the stress budget B = 100 (canonical footing; alt +91). The lensing relation continues past every budget the galaxies have. THIS KILLS L247's medium as a source of the lensing signal, and every reading in which the phantom carrying the lensing IS the galaxy's own bounded sector)

V4 -- the same budget, radius-resolved, on the lensing rotation curves (four stellar-mass bins)
      (bin 1 spans log M* = 8.5-10.3, too wide for a representative mass; the verdict below rests on bins 2-4)
    bin 1 (log M* = 9.40): M_bar = 3.27e+09, AM halo 1.51e+11, B = 45.3; at R = 762 kpc the lensing mass is 1468 M_bar = 31.68 of the whole abundance-matching budget
    bin 2 (log M* = 10.45): M_bar = 3.66e+10, AM halo 7.64e+11, B = 19.8; at R = 762 kpc the lensing mass is 181 M_bar = 8.67 of the whole abundance-matching budget
    bin 3 (log M* = 10.70): M_bar = 6.52e+10, AM halo 2.01e+12, B = 29.9; at R = 762 kpc the lensing mass is 125 M_bar = 4.05 of the whole abundance-matching budget
    bin 4 (log M* = 10.90): M_bar = 1.03e+11, AM halo 5.99e+12, B = 57.0; at R = 762 kpc the lensing mass is 89 M_bar = 1.54 of the whole abundance-matching budget
  [PASS] V4 [THE BUDGET IS ALREADY OVERSPENT INSIDE ONE MEGAPARSEC] the enclosed lensing mass at the outermost bin inside 1 Mpc is compared, bin by bin, with the whole abundance-matching budget of the same galaxies; a ratio above one means the lensing signal has already claimed more mass than the galaxies own
           (3 of the 3 narrow mass bins exceed their entire budget inside 1 Mpc (fractions 31.68, 8.67, 4.05, 1.54). The excess is real mass in the universe -- in the standard picture the two-halo term of correlated neighbours -- but it is NOT bound to the lens, so no reading in which the lensing phantom is the galaxy's OWN equilibrated sector can claim it)

V5 -- the honest limitation: what correlated structure can mask
    [canonical] for log M* = 10.6 the deep-branch phantom density drops to the cosmic mean matter density at r = 3.42 Mpc, i.e. g_bar = 6.15e-16 m/s^2 -- beyond that radius the claimed phantom is below the background and the excess-surface-density estimator cannot see it as an excess
    [alt] for log M* = 10.6 the deep-branch phantom density drops to the cosmic mean matter density at r = 3.59 Mpc, i.e. g_bar = 5.61e-16 m/s^2 -- beyond that radius the claimed phantom is below the background and the excess-surface-density estimator cannot see it as an excess
    dropping the 3 lowest-acceleration bins (12 left, 5 of them still below the truncation): Delta chi2 = +199.4
    dropping the 5 lowest-acceleration bins (10 left, 3 of them still below the truncation): Delta chi2 = +74.2
    dropping the 7 lowest-acceleration bins (8 left, 1 of them still below the truncation): Delta chi2 = +4.9
  [FAIL] V5 [THE VERDICT SURVIVES DROPPING THE BINS MOST EXPOSED TO CORRELATED STRUCTURE] the lowest-acceleration bins -- the largest radii, where neighbouring haloes contribute most to the excess surface density and the lens's own one-halo term is weakest -- are removed in three increasingly severe cuts and the two models recompared on what is left
           (Delta chi2 = +199 / +74 / +5 after dropping 3 / 5 / 7 bins. The FAIL at seven is a loss of POWER, not a reversal: seven cuts leave only one bin below the truncation, so the regime the test probes is gone. The honest scope is the first two cuts, which keep 5 and 3 bins below the turn and still exclude it; the verdict does depend on the low-acceleration bins, because that is the only place a mass-budget truncation can show itself)

V6 -- the scope this leaves for a capped equilibrium reading
    [canonical] external-field cap radius for a log M* = 10.6 lens: r_cap = 5.8 kpc; the lensing data run 35 kpc to 3000 kpc, so the capped equilibrium covers 0% of the measured range in log radius
    [alt] external-field cap radius for a log M* = 10.6 lens: r_cap = 5.8 kpc; the lensing data run 35 kpc to 3000 kpc, so the capped equilibrium covers 0% of the measured range in log radius
  [PASS] V6 [A CAPPED EQUILIBRIUM READING SURVIVES THIS TEST ONLY BY MAKING NO PREDICTION WHERE THE DATA ARE] the external-field cap radius is computed for a lens of the sample's median mass and compared with the radii the lensing measurement covers; a fraction at or near zero means the confined phantom is not the object the lensing signal measures, and the free outer component carries all of it
           (the cap sits at 6 kpc, BELOW the innermost lensing bin at 35 kpc: the confined phantom covers none of the measured range. A capped reading therefore evades this kill, at the stated price that ordinary cold collisionless matter carries 100% of the lensing signal these data measure, and the identification makes no prediction anywhere in that range)

L248 COMPLETE: 5/6 checks PASS.
